  </p>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Why it mattered</h2>
  <p class="mb-5 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    The bottleneck was never the analysts' judgment &mdash; it was how long it took them to get a clean, decision-ready view of a deal. A faster manual process would still have meant a person reading through filings line by line. Rapid Investment needed the synthesis itself to happen automatically, so the first thing an analyst sees is already a structured picture of the opportunity, not a stack of raw documents to work through before the real analysis can start.
  </p>
  <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#76B900] pl-4 text-[15px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]">
    &ldquo;The model is the easy part. What actually mattered was getting the data pulled together before an analyst even opens the file.&rdquo;
    <span class="mt-2 block not-italic text-[13px] text-navy-400">&mdash; Head of Research, Rapid Investment</span>
  </blockquote>
</div>

<div class="rounded-2xl border border-navy-100/60 bg-white p-8 shadow-subtle" data-reveal>
  <blockquote class="mb-4 text-[19px] italic leading-relaxed text-[#111827]">
    &ldquo;We used to lose good opportunities to the clock. Now our analysts start from a synthesized view of the deal instead of a stack of raw documents, and we move on time-sensitive deals we would have missed before.&rdquo;
  </blockquote>
  <p class="text-[14px] text-[#6B7280]">
    <strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Head of Research</strong><br>
    Rapid Investment
  </p>
</div>

